            <title>[LU-21316] sanity-quota test_84: grant is not cleared after quota reset on ZFS</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21316</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/eda1ac26-dbb5-41a7-95cf-fb4683853af0" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/eda1ac26-dbb5-41a7-95cf-fb4683853af0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_84 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;grant is not cleared
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.120&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137656" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137656&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 4.18.0-553.177.1.el8_10.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.120&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137656" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137656&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 4.18.0-553.177.1.el8_10_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-quota test_84 (ZFS) fails at "grant is not cleared" (sanity-quota.sh, after the final "lfs setquota -g quota_usr -r" and a 3 s sleep): OST0000 still reports the insane group bhardlimit 18446744073707374604 for gid 60000 although the MDT-side reset was done. The test's own wait loop ("wait N seconds for OBDs to reset the quota ID 60000") ran 31 s and ended with "fail to reset the quota ID 60000 on OBDs", so this is not a short timing window: OST0000 never picked up the reset. OST0001 and the MDT showed 0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/735dd8f9-83ff-4c93-a02c-f4e623b5ef90" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/735dd8f9-83ff-4c93-a02c-f4e623b5ef90&lt;/a&gt; (review-zfs, el8.10, master 1931825a3cf4, &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/71296" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/71296&lt;/a&gt; PS2, a ptlrpc tracepoint patch that does not touch quota). Same error on a Janitor sanity-quota-zfs run of change 71435 on 2026-11-22. Rate: 10 failures in about 1390 review-zfs runs in 30 days for test_84 overall (all signatures).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21223" title="sanity-quota test_84: dd succeed, expect EDQUOT after quota reset on ZFS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21223"&gt;LU-21223&lt;/a&gt;: that ticket is "dd succeed, expect EDQUOT" at the later limit check, and its fix (change 71102, wait_quota_synced before the dd) does not touch the grant-cleared check. Not &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16529" title="sanity-quota test_84: pool grant is not set as insane value" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16529"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16529&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (pool grant is not set as insane value): that is an earlier check, and its fix 50799 is in the tested tree. Possibly related to the same reintegration/sync weakness on ZFS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-71296-ps2-edeb34cba77d on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/71296" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/71296&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
